NV_PK(11,{"this is the front hall the temple's main gate the ends of the roof curve up like swallow tails and colorful figures and dragons stand on the ridge":"","a stone lion stands at the gate behind it a dragon wraps around a stone column":"","this dark stele is the one shi lang set up in 1685 a dragon is carved at the top and the words are painted red the first line on the right says taiwan is far across the sea":"","big characters are written on the walls between the halls here you see respect for parents and loyalty with a round painting between them":"","on the other wall is the character for integrity and another round painting the colorful weapons below are ceremonial weapons set out to show respect for mazu":"","this is also a wall anchor shaped like a ruyi a lucky symbol that means 'as you wish'":"","shi lang set it up in 1685 it is one of the oldest stone steles in taiwan the words are shi lang's own account told from the qing side the stele says taiwan was far across the sea the dutch came in the late ming years then koxinga took taiwan and his family ruled it for generations in 1683 shi lang won a battle at penghu landed at luermen and accepted the surrender he ordered his soldiers not to harm the people anyone who took even one thread from them would be punished then he asked the court to set up one prefecture and three counties and to cut taxes by half":"","on his stele what did shi lang say he ordered his soldiers not to do":"","take anything from the people":"","sail at night":"","pray to mazu":"","leave their ships":"","the stele says anyone who took even one thread from the people would be punished":"","the walls show big characters such as loyalty respect for parents and integrity":""});